{"name":"Physalis","hex":"#ef9548","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Physalis","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Solanaceae – groundcherries, including some called gooseberries and Chinese lantern."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Physalis"}],"entries":[{"title":"Physalis","blocks":[{"text":"Physalis is a genus of approximately 75 to 90 flowering plants in the nightshade family (Solanaceae), which are native to the Americas and Australasia. At least 46 species are endemic to Mexico. Cultivated and weedy species have been introduced worldwide. A defining feature of Physalis is a large, papery husk derived from the calyx, which partly or fully encloses the fruit. Many species bear edible fruit, and some species are cultivated."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Starr_061225-2955_Physalis_peruviana.jpg/330px-Starr_061225-2955_Physalis_peruviana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Physalis","wikidata":"Q158663"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Physalis_peruviana_calix_open_close-up.jpg/500px-Physalis_peruviana_calix_open_close-up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Physalis_peruviana_calix_open_close-up.jpg/1280px-Physalis_peruviana_calix_open_close-up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Physalis_peruviana_calix_open_close-up.jpg/500px-Physalis_peruviana_calix_open_close-up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Physalis peruviana fruit with calyx open","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhysalis_peruviana_calix_open_close-up.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/w